<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Atil</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Atil was the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khazar-khaganate">Khazar Khaganate</a>, located on the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volga">Volga</a> near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caspian-sea">Caspian Sea</a>. It was a major trading centre, with communities of different religions, and the seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khagan">khagan</a> and the government. It was destroyed by the Rus' prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sviatoslav-i-of-kiev">Sviatoslav</a> in the 960s, contributing to the Khazars' decline.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/atil.jpg" alt="Atil" width="320" height="222" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Briangotts · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Varangian_routes.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
